    <string name="chart_about_temperatures">The room temperature against the target of the active program (dashed) and the outside temperature. Rooms that stay below the dashed line in cold weather point at a heating curve that is too low.</string>
    <string name="chart_about_supply">The water temperature leaving the boiler against the setpoint from the heating curve (dashed). Lower is more efficient: a condensing boiler condenses best below about 55 °C.</string>
    <string name="chart_about_modulation">How hard the burner works (share of its maximum power). Long phases at low modulation are efficient; many short peaks mean frequent starts.</string>
    <string name="chart_about_pressure">Water pressure of the heating system. It moves a little with temperature; a steady drop over days can mean air or a small leak.</string>
    <string name="chart_about_gas">Gas used for heating, from the boiler\'s daily counter. Compare days with similar outside temperatures to see the effect of a setting change.</string>
    <string name="chart_about_burner">How long the burner was running. Per day it uses the boiler\'s hour counter (whole hours); for 24 h it is estimated from the burner state at each refresh.</string>
